{"v":15,"id":"e09","kid":"emma","title":"Terry Fox and the Marathon of Hope","zh":"特里·福克斯与\"希望马拉松\"","level":"B1","genre":"人物传记 · 北美","src":"facts","sum":"加拿大青年特里·福克斯因骨癌失去一条腿，却装着假肢横跨加拿大长跑，为癌症研究募款。他没能跑完，但每年的\"特里·福克斯长跑\"延续了他的梦想。","words":297,"paras":[{"t":"Every September, people all over Canada go out to run, walk or ride their bikes in the Terry Fox Run. They are remembering a young man who showed the world what courage looks like.","w":[[0,5,"every",-1],[6,15,"september",-1],[17,23,"people",-1],[24,27,"all",-1],[28,32,"over",-1],[33,39,"canada",-1],[40,42,"go",-1],[43,46,"out",-1],[47,49,"to",-1],[50,53,"run",-1],[55,59,"walk",-1],[60,62,"or",-1],[63,67,"ride",-1],[68,73,"their",-1],[74,79,"bikes",-1],[80,82,"in",-1],[83,86,"the",-1],[87,92,"Terry",0],[93,96,"Fox",0],[97,100,"Run",0],[102,106,"they",-1],[107,110,"are",-1],[111,122,"remembering",-1],[123,124,"a",-1],[125,130,"young",-1],[131,134,"man",-1],[135,138,"who",-1],[139,145,"showed",-1],[146,149,"the",-1],[150,155,"world",-1],[156,160,"what",17],[161,168,"courage",17],[169,174,"looks",17],[175,179,"like",17]]},{"t":"Terry Fox was born in 1958 and grew up in British Columbia, a province on Canada's west coast. He loved sports, especially basketball. When he was 18, doctors found that he had bone cancer in his right leg. To save his life, the leg had to be removed above the knee. He then learned to walk and run with an artificial leg.","w":[[0,5,"Terry",-1],[6,9,"Fox",-1],[10,13,"was",-1],[14,18,"born",-1],[19,21,"in",-1],[27,30,"and",-1],[31,35,"grew",-1],[36,38,"up",-1],[39,41,"in",-1],[42,49,"British",2],[50,58,"Columbia",2],[60,61,"a",-1],[62,70,"province",-1],[71,73,"on",-1],[74,82,"canada's",-1],[83,87,"west",3],[88,93,"coast",3],[95,97,"he",-1],[98,103,"loved",-1],[104,110,"sports",-1],[112,122,"especially",-1],[123,133,"basketball",-1],[135,139,"when",-1],[140,142,"he",-1],[143,146,"was",-1],[151,158,"doctors",-1],[159,164,"found",-1],[165,169,"that",-1],[170,172,"he",-1],[173,176,"had",-1],[177,181,"bone",4],[182,188,"cancer",4],[189,191,"in",-1],[192,195,"his",-1],[196,201,"right",-1],[202,205,"leg",-1],[207,209,"to",-1],[210,214,"save",-1],[215,218,"his",-1],[219,223,"life",-1],[225,228,"the",-1],[229,232,"leg",-1],[233,236,"had",-1],[237,239,"to",-1],[240,242,"be",-1],[243,250,"removed",-1],[251,256,"above",-1],[257,260,"the",-1],[261,265,"knee",-1],[267,269,"he",-1],[270,274,"then",-1],[275,282,"learned",-1],[283,285,"to",-1],[286,290,"walk",-1],[291,294,"and",-1],[295,298,"run",-1],[299,303,"with",-1],[304,306,"an",-1],[307,317,"artificial",5],[318,321,"leg",5]]},{"t":"In the hospital, Terry saw many other patients, including young children, who were suffering from cancer. He decided to do something big to help. He planned to run across the whole of Canada, from the Atlantic Ocean to the Pacific Ocean, to raise money for cancer research. He called it the Marathon of Hope.","w":[[0,2,"in",-1],[3,6,"the",-1],[7,15,"hospital",-1],[17,22,"Terry",-1],[23,26,"saw",-1],[27,31,"many",-1],[32,37,"other",-1],[38,46,"patients",-1],[48,57,"including",-1],[58,63,"young",-1],[64,72,"children",-1],[74,77,"who",-1],[78,82,"were",-1],[83,92,"suffering",6],[93,97,"from",6],[98,104,"cancer",-1],[106,108,"he",-1],[109,116,"decided",-1],[117,119,"to",-1],[120,122,"do",-1],[123,132,"something",-1],[133,136,"big",-1],[137,139,"to",-1],[140,144,"help",-1],[146,148,"he",-1],[149,156,"planned",-1],[157,159,"to",-1],[160,163,"run",-1],[164,170,"across",-1],[171,174,"the",-1],[175,180,"whole",-1],[181,183,"of",-1],[184,190,"canada",-1],[192,196,"from",-1],[197,200,"the",-1],[201,209,"atlantic",9],[210,215,"ocean",9],[216,218,"to",-1],[219,222,"the",-1],[223,230,"pacific",10],[231,236,"ocean",10],[238,240,"to",-1],[241,246,"raise",7],[247,252,"money",7],[253,256,"for",-1],[257,263,"cancer",8],[264,272,"research",8],[274,276,"he",-1],[277,283,"called",-1],[284,286,"it",-1],[287,290,"the",-1],[291,299,"Marathon",1],[300,302,"of",1],[303,307,"hope",1]]},{"t":"On April 12, 1980, Terry dipped his artificial leg in the Atlantic Ocean in St. John's, Newfoundland, and began to run. Almost every day, he ran about 42 kilometers, the length of a marathon. He ran through rain, strong winds and summer heat. At first, few people noticed him. But soon crowds were waiting along the roads to cheer for him, and people donated money in every town.","w":[[0,2,"on",-1],[3,8,"april",-1],[19,24,"Terry",-1],[25,31,"dipped",-1],[32,35,"his",-1],[36,46,"artificial",5],[47,50,"leg",5],[51,53,"in",-1],[54,57,"the",-1],[58,66,"atlantic",9],[67,72,"ocean",9],[73,75,"in",-1],[76,79,"St",11],[80,86,"John's",11],[88,100,"Newfoundland",-1],[102,105,"and",-1],[106,111,"began",-1],[112,114,"to",-1],[115,118,"run",-1],[120,126,"almost",-1],[127,132,"every",-1],[133,136,"day",-1],[138,140,"he",-1],[141,144,"ran",-1],[145,150,"about",-1],[154,164,"kilometers",-1],[166,169,"the",-1],[170,176,"length",-1],[177,179,"of",-1],[180,181,"a",-1],[182,190,"marathon",-1],[192,194,"he",-1],[195,198,"ran",-1],[199,206,"through",-1],[207,211,"rain",-1],[213,219,"strong",-1],[220,225,"winds",-1],[226,229,"and",-1],[230,236,"summer",-1],[237,241,"heat",-1],[243,245,"at",-1],[246,251,"first",-1],[253,256,"few",-1],[257,263,"people",-1],[264,271,"noticed",-1],[272,275,"him",-1],[277,280,"but",-1],[281,285,"soon",-1],[286,292,"crowds",-1],[293,297,"were",-1],[298,305,"waiting",-1],[306,311,"along",-1],[312,315,"the",-1],[316,321,"roads",-1],[322,324,"to",-1],[325,330,"cheer",13],[331,334,"for",13],[335,338,"him",-1],[340,343,"and",-1],[344,350,"people",-1],[351,358,"donated",-1],[359,364,"money",-1],[365,367,"in",-1],[368,373,"every",-1],[374,378,"town",-1]]},{"t":"After 143 days and 5,373 kilometers, Terry had to stop near Thunder Bay, Ontario. The cancer had spread to his lungs. He died the next year, in June 1981, at the age of 22.","w":[[0,5,"after",-1],[10,14,"days",-1],[15,18,"and",-1],[25,35,"kilometers",-1],[37,42,"Terry",-1],[43,46,"had",-1],[47,49,"to",-1],[50,54,"stop",-1],[55,59,"near",-1],[60,67,"Thunder",12],[68,71,"Bay",12],[73,80,"Ontario",-1],[82,85,"the",-1],[86,92,"cancer",-1],[93,96,"had",-1],[97,103,"spread",-1],[104,106,"to",-1],[107,110,"his",-1],[111,116,"lungs",-1],[118,120,"he",-1],[121,125,"died",-1],[126,129,"the",-1],[130,134,"next",-1],[135,139,"year",-1],[141,143,"in",-1],[144,148,"june",-1],[155,157,"at",14],[158,161,"the",14],[162,165,"age",14],[166,168,"of",14]]},{"t":"Terry never finished his run, but his dream did not end. The first Terry Fox Run was held in 1981, and since then the runs have raised hundreds of millions of dollars for cancer research. Terry once said, \"Even if I don't finish, we need others to continue.\" Millions of people have done exactly that.","w":[[0,5,"Terry",-1],[6,11,"never",-1],[12,20,"finished",-1],[21,24,"his",-1],[25,28,"run",-1],[30,33,"but",-1],[34,37,"his",-1],[38,43,"dream",-1],[44,47,"did",-1],[48,51,"not",-1],[52,55,"end",-1],[57,60,"the",-1],[61,66,"first",-1],[67,72,"Terry",0],[73,76,"Fox",0],[77,80,"Run",0],[81,84,"was",-1],[85,89,"held",-1],[90,92,"in",-1],[99,102,"and",-1],[103,108,"since",-1],[109,113,"then",-1],[114,117,"the",-1],[118,122,"runs",-1],[123,127,"have",-1],[128,134,"raised",-1],[135,143,"hundreds",16],[144,146,"of",16],[147,155,"millions",16],[156,158,"of",16],[159,166,"dollars",-1],[167,170,"for",-1],[171,177,"cancer",8],[178,186,"research",8],[188,193,"Terry",-1],[194,198,"once",-1],[199,203,"said",-1],[206,210,"even",15],[211,213,"if",15],[214,215,"i",-1],[216,221,"don't",-1],[222,228,"finish",-1],[230,232,"we",-1],[233,237,"need",-1],[238,244,"others",-1],[245,247,"to",-1],[248,256,"continue",-1],[259,267,"millions",-1],[268,270,"of",-1],[271,277,"people",-1],[278,282,"have",-1],[283,287,"done",-1],[288,295,"exactly",-1],[296,300,"that",-1]]}],"gl":{"every":["every","/ˈevəri/","adj. 每个的，每一的","level"],"september":["september","/sepˈtembər/","n. 九月","level"],"people":["people","/ˈpipəl/","n. 人们","override"],"all":["all","/ɔl/","det. 全部，所有","override"],"over":["over","/